TEXT -2048 -616 Left 5 ;This example shows a model of a 9-bus three-phase power system network. \nAfter 5s a pure active power load of 50MW is switched to the network \nThis example is based on an IEEE® benchmark test case, further details of which can be found in \n"Power System Control and Stability" by P. M. Anderson and A. A. Fouad (IEEE Press, 2003).  \nThe resulting load flow solution is computed\nLooking at Bus 1, it can be seen that the swing generator delivers 75.8MW \nof active power and 26.0MVAr or reactive power to the network. \nDifferences to the original benchmark are due to the transmission line models \nand transformer configurations used.
